{"kind":"artifact","text":"Scale evidence page at docs/reference/performance.md plus its docs/README.md index entry, re-measured at main adda28c8 after five of the six bounded requests this work raised were merged. Under the current commitment lifecycle this artifact is the implementation report for promise ee10b719; no separate ready-for-review report is filed. Both envelope depths are now measured directly rather than extrapolated, because the harness merged as 84805b04 builds a 50,000-record fixture in 55 s and a 500,000-record one in 80 s and carries depth, actor-count and fan-out axes. Envelopes, unchanged and still written before any measurement: PREVIEW 50,000 records, 8 actors, fan-out p99 8 max 64, 128 MiB checkpoint; FIRST-PRODUCTION 500,000, 50, p99 16 max 256, 256 MiB, with the halving assumption behind 500,000 stated explicitly and the undiscounted 1.06 million named. Measured at main adda28c8, load 2.5 to 5: cold verify of this repository 1.69 s with 6 git subprocesses at depth 6,205; harness cold audit 184.6 ms, 12.80 s and 128.7 s at depths 100, 50,000 and 500,000; resident startup without a usable checkpoint 12.83 s and 127.4 s at 50,000 and 500,000; checkpoint restart 178.1 ms, 733.2 ms, 11.95 s, 11.93 s and 46.30 s at tails 0, 10, 255, 256 and 1000; warm status on the bounded route 11.0, 15.7 and 103.3 ms at depths 5,000, 50,000 and 500,000 with a response of 726 to 732 B throughout; live resident full route 11,978,253 B in 23 ms against bounded route 31,879 B in 14 ms; checkpoint blob 1,781,504 B at depth 6,205, or 287 B per record, in the v3 format; warm resident peak RSS 135, 937 and 9,183 MB at 5,000, 50,000 and 500,000, a slope of 17.8 KB per record; fan-out axis incremental 0.22 ms per base from 1 to 256 at depth 50,000; actor count at equal record count 308.6 ms for 1 actor against 303.0 ms for 50 over 7 repeats. Verdicts. Passing: cold verify at both envelopes, 12.8 s and 2.1 min, flipped from miss by merge 06594a3b; checkpoint blob at both, about 14 MB and 144 MB, flipped at FIRST-PRODUCTION by merge d62e5e17 and still missing at 1.06 million; warm status on the ordinary bounded route at both, flipped from not-established and from miss by merges 84805b04 and adda28c8; resident RSS at PREVIEW, 937 MB against 1 GiB with 12 percent headroom, flipped by merge 5fc9929c; actor count at both; and restart at FIRST-PRODUCTION. Missing honestly: resident RSS at FIRST-PRODUCTION, 9.18 GB against 4 GiB; the max-fan-out target as written, about 774 ms against 50 ms, while fan-out width itself costs 0.22 ms per base; and cold restart at PREVIEW, 11.95 s against 10 s. That last one is the finding the merges did not move, and it was re-measured on a quiet machine to check: at the same depth 512 a checkpointed restart with a 255-record tail takes 11.95 s while a full cold audit of the whole repository takes 0.30 s, both reproducing to within 0.2 percent, so the checkpoint is about 40 times slower than not having one and only begins to pay near 47,000 records. The whole-projection route is recorded as not applicable rather than as a miss, because it is now an explicit opt-in that is uncapped by design. Two figures remain extrapolated and say so in place: restart from a checkpoint at FIRST-PRODUCTION depth, because every contract checkpoint case places its checkpoint at depth 257; and response sizes at envelope depth, taken from this repository's real 1,930 B per record rather than the fixture's inflated 6.4 KB. Gates at this exact head: go build, go vet, go test ./internal/docset -count=1 in 95.6 s, and go test ./... -count=1 all pass; the root README public-surface failure reported in earlier rounds is fixed on main and the tree is green. Nothing was fixed inline and no invariant was weakened.","body":{"commit":"18bbedf4c329a980d7497ff5773b6690866c486d","path":"docs"}}